    <string name="fraud_prevention_tips_title">Fraud Prevention Tips</string>
    <string name="fraud_prevention_tips_body">1. Guard Your Identity and Access\n• Enable Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA): Use MFA on all banking, social media, and email accounts. Prioritize authenticator apps or biometrics over SMS-based codes when possible.\n• Verify urgent requests: If you receive a call or message claiming to be an authority figure, hang up and call back using a verified number from the official website or your saved contacts.\n\n2. Practice Good Cyber Hygiene\n• Unique passwords: Use a password manager to generate and store complex, unique passwords for every account.\n• Limit public oversharing: Be mindful of personal info (birthdays, locations, workplaces) you share on social media.\n\n3. The Golden Rule of SMS\n• Never click links: Banks, government agencies (SSS or BIR), and major couriers (Lalamove or Grab) will not send clickable links in an SMS for sensitive verification or payment issues.\n• Do not reply to scams: Do not reply \"STOP\" or \"NO\" to suspicious texts. Replying confirms your number is active.\n\n4. Use Built-In Protection Features\n• Google Messages (Android): Enable Spam Protection to automatically move suspicious messages to a separate folder.\n• Apple Messages (iOS): Enable Filter Unknown Senders in Settings &gt; Messages.</string>
